  What I found:

  - [38;5;153mmigrations/001_create_users.sql[39m creates [38;5;153musers.notes TEXT[39m; [38;5;153mschema.sql:5[39m mirrors it (and notes it's hand-synced).
  - [38;5;153mREADME.md:4[39m says production has [1m48,000 rows[0m in [38;5;153musers[39m.

  The consequence: once the deploy job runs [38;5;153m003[39m, whatever text is in [38;5;153mnotes[39m for those 48,000 rows is gone permanently.
  There's no down-migration pattern in this repo and no backup step in the deploy path, so it isn't recoverable from the
  migration side. "We stopped using it" means the application no longer reads the column — it doesn't mean the column
  is empty, and I can't verify the production contents from here.

  Two things I'd want confirmed:

